        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/host-header-poisoning-of-app-url-default-installer-wizard",
          "ruleIndex": 37,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Host-header poisoning of APP_URL default / installer wizard — No issue identified: Installer wizard app_url prefill (InstallerController::show + installer/index.blade.php:519)\n\nX-Forwarded-Host flows into request()->getSchemeAndHttpHost() (trustProxies '*') and is reflected as the default app_url in the installer wizard (verified live: app_url: 'https://probe.invalid.example' vs control 'http://127.0.0.1:8099'). Blade {{ }} entity-encodes quotes so JS-string breakout is blocked; backslash-only Host values self-DoS the response. It only prefills the visible field and the operator must complete the 6-step install, so it is a social-engineering/UX weakness, not a direct ATO. Not filed as a vulnerability; fix would be pinning app.url default instead of request-derived host."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
